{"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","modules":[{"name":"SwiftML"}],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Early Stopping & Generalization Control"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Training-Callbacks","title":"Training Callbacks","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/EarlyStopping","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/MetricDirection"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftml\/earlystoppingcallbacks"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Halt iterative training dynamically when validation performance ceases to improve to prevent overfitting.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","title":"Guides & Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/SupervisedClassifiers","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/SupervisedRegressors","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/EnsembleLearning","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/HistogramGradientBoosting","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/ReproducibilityAndPRNG","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/MLOpsExport"],"generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/EarlyStoppingCallbacks","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterative estimators like multi-layer perceptrons ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLPClassifier"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLPRegressor"},{"type":"text","text":") and gradient boosted decision trees ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GradientBoostedTreesRegressor"},{"type":"text","text":") improve their training loss over successive iterations. However, after sufficient capacity has been fit, additional epochs frequently lead to overfitting on training noise and deteriorating generalization on unseen data."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EarlyStopping"},{"type":"text","text":" provides a decoupled, value-type training callback that monitors validation loss or performance metrics across successive epochs, halting training and optionally restoring optimal model weights."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Mechanics--State-Machine","text":"Mechanics & State Machine","type":"heading"},{"syntax":null,"code":["Epoch Evaluation (Score S_t)","            │","            ▼"," Is (Best - S_t) > minDelta?","   ├── YES ──► Reset wait = 0, update bestScore = S_t, checkpoint weights","   └── NO  ──► Increment wait = wait + 1","                 │","            Is wait >= patience?","              ├── YES ──► shouldStop = true, restore best checkpoint weights","              └── NO  ──► Continue training"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Configuration-Parameters","text":"Configuration Parameters","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"patience","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": Number of consecutive non-improving evaluations tolerated before triggering an early halt.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"minDelta","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": Minimum absolute improvement required to qualify as progress.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"direction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":".minimize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for loss functions (cross-entropy, MSE) or ","type":"text"},{"code":".maximize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for scoring metrics (accuracy, R2, AUC).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"restoreBestWeights","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": When ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", automatically restores the model parameters from the epoch that achieved ","type":"text"},{"code":"bestScore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", avoiding overfit tail iterations.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Example-Usage","text":"Example Usage","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftML","","\/\/ 1. Configure early stopping callback","let es = EarlyStopping(","    patience: 5,","    minDelta: 1e-4,","    direction: .minimize,","    restoreBestWeights: true",")","","\/\/ 2. Fit MLP with validation monitoring","let mlp = MLPClassifier(hiddenLayerSizes: [32, 16], maxIter: 200)","try await mlp.fit(","    features: X_train,","    targets: y_train,","    validationFeatures: X_val,","    validationTargets: y_val,","    earlyStopping: es",")"],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://SwiftML/documentation/SwiftML/SupervisedRegressors":{"kind":"article","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Perform continuous target predictions using LinearRegression (exact OLS), DecisionTreeRegressor, and GradientBoostedTreesRegressor."}],"type":"topic","title":"Supervised Regression Models","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/SupervisedRegressors","url":"\/documentation\/swiftml\/supervisedregressors"},"doc://SwiftML/documentation/SwiftML/EnsembleLearning":{"kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Train high-accuracy bagging and boosting decision tree ensembles natively in Swift with multicore parallelism."}],"type":"topic","title":"Ensemble Learning: Random Forests & Gradient Boosted Trees","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/EnsembleLearning","url":"\/documentation\/swiftml\/ensemblelearning"},"doc://SwiftML/documentation/SwiftML":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Supervised Machine Learning Estimators & Neural Networks."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftml","type":"topic","title":"SwiftML"},"d